A refund ledger totals a signed adjustment with this helper.
static int total(int n) {
  if (n == 0) return 0;
  return n + total(n - 1);
}
The caller passes total(-1) for a one-unit refund. What actually happens?

This helper is meant to report the largest reading in a range.
static int biggest(int[] a, int lo, int hi) {
  if (lo > hi) return 0;
  int rest = biggest(a, lo + 1, hi);
  return Math.max(a[lo], rest);
}
Run biggest(new int[]{-5, -9, -2}, 0, 2). What comes back?

A totaliser walks an array from a given start index.
static int from(int[] a, int i) {
  if (i == 1) return 0;
  return a[i - 1] + from(a, i - 1);
}
The caller runs from(weights, 0) on an array of length 3. What happens?

A digit checker wraps its argument before recursing.
static int wrapped(int n) {
  if (n == 0) return 0;
  return 1 + wrapped(n % 3);
}
Instrument the method and run wrapped(7). What argument sequence does it see?

Fill the blank so the helper reports the largest value in a range, including ranges whose values are all negative.
static int biggest(int[] a, int lo, int hi) {
  if (lo > hi) return /* blank */;
  return Math.max(a[lo], biggest(a, lo + 1, hi));
}

A formatter joins labels from the back of an array toward the front.
static String label(String[] a, int i) {
  if (i == a.length) return null;
  return a[i] + label(a, i + 1);
}
Run label(new String[]{"a", "b", "c"}, 0). What string is produced?

Instrument every invocation of this helper, the first one included.
static int split(int n) {
  if (n == 0) return 0;
  return 1 + split(n - 1) + split(n - 2 < 0 ? 0 : n - 2);
}
How many invocations occur for split(5)?

A spell checker looks for a vowel in a word.
static boolean hasVowel(String s, int i) {
  if (i == s.length()) return false;
  if ("aeiou".indexOf(s.charAt(i)) >= 0) return true;
  return hasVowel(s.substring(i), 0);
}
Run hasVowel("xay", 0). What happens?

